package api

var sswCurriculumFisheryBodies3English = map[examSSWEnglishKey]string{
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Kepadatan memengaruhi akses pakan, kualitas air, pertumbuhan, dan risiko stres. Target bergantung spesies, ukuran, sarana, dan kapasitas pengelolaan air. Grading memisahkan ukuran bila diperlukan dengan alat dan waktu penanganan yang sesuai. Jumlah hidup dihitung dari data awal, penambahan, pemindahan, serta kematian yang dicatat; angka perkiraan harus dibedakan dari hitungan pasti. Jangan menaikkan kepadatan hanya karena ruang tampak masih luas atau menghapus mortalitas agar catatan terlihat baik.`}:                                                `Stocking density affects access to feed, water quality, growth, and stress risk. Targets depend on species, size, facilities, and water-management capacity. When needed, grading separates size groups using suitable equipment and handling times. Calculate live counts from starting data, additions, transfers, and recorded mortalities; distinguish estimates from exact counts. Do not increase density just because space appears available or omit mortalities to make records look better.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Kesegaran dipengaruhi waktu, suhu, kerusakan fisik, serta pencemaran. Gunakan wadah dan es yang sesuai penggunaan, hindari kontak produk bersih dengan bahan bakar, limbah, atau alat kotor. Pendinginan dilakukan sesuai spesies serta metode fasilitas; satu rasio es tidak berlaku untuk semua kondisi. Jangan menganggap bau normal membuktikan produk aman. Ikan berduri atau berbahaya memerlukan penanganan khusus. Pisahkan hasil rusak atau meragukan untuk penilaian berwenang sebelum pengiriman.`}:                                                           `Freshness is affected by time, temperature, physical damage, and contamination. Use containers and ice suitable for their intended use; keep clean products away from fuel, waste, and dirty equipment. Cool products according to the species and facility method; one ice ratio does not fit every condition. A normal smell does not prove a product is safe. Spiny or hazardous fish require special handling. Isolate damaged or questionable catch for an authorized assessment before shipment.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Kesiapan panen memerlukan kondisi organisme, target mutu, status perlakuan, kebutuhan pasar, serta sarana penanganan. Catatan obat dan masa henti yang berlaku harus dikonfirmasi sebelum produk dikirim; penampilan sehat tidak cukup. Penghentian pakan sebelum panen, bila diperlukan, mengikuti rencana spesies dan fasilitas. Jangan menganggap satu lama penghentian berlaku untuk semua. Siapkan alat serta wadah bersih dan posisi pekerja aman, lalu tangani organisme dengan metode terlatih untuk mengurangi cedera serta penurunan mutu.`}:                   `Harvest readiness depends on stock condition, quality targets, treatment status, market needs, and handling facilities. Confirm medication records and any applicable withdrawal period before shipping; a healthy appearance is not enough. If feed must be withheld before harvest, follow the species and facility plan. Do not assume one withholding period applies to every case. Prepare clean equipment and containers, work from a safe position, and use trained handling methods to reduce injury and quality loss.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Komunikasi di kapal harus singkat dan dipahami, terutama perintah berhenti, bahaya, arah, serta lokasi awak. 止まって berarti berhenti dan 危険 berarti bahaya. Jika instruksi tidak terdengar, minta pengulangan; jangan mengira semua teriakan meminta mempercepat. Laporan berisi kondisi alat, lokasi, waktu, dan tindakan yang telah diambil. Bahasa Jepang dipelajari bersama demonstrasi aman serta latihan kapal, bukan menggantikan pelatihan navigasi atau radio. Dalam ujian resmi perikanan, bahasa Jepang menjadi bagian penting pemahaman soal.`}:                `Communication aboard a vessel should be brief and understood, especially commands to stop, warnings, directions, and crew locations. 止まって means “stop,” and 危険 means “danger.” If you do not hear an instruction, ask for it to be repeated; do not assume every shout means “speed up.” Reports include equipment condition, location, time, and actions taken. Learn Japanese alongside safe demonstrations and vessel drills; it does not replace navigation or radio training. Japanese is an important part of understanding questions in the official fisheries examination.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Laporan unit memuat spesies atau kelompok, waktu, parameter air, pakan aktual, mortalitas, pemindahan, serta tindakan yang telah disetujui. 給餌量 adalah jumlah pakan dan 水温 adalah suhu air. Ketidakjelasan satuan dapat mengubah keputusan; minta pengulangan dan konfirmasikan angka sebelum tindakan. Bedakan data ukur dari perkiraan. Ujian resmi budi daya menggunakan bahasa Jepang, sedangkan materi ini memberi jembatan Indonesia dengan kosakata dan kasus. Pemahaman tertulis tidak menggantikan pelatihan pengukuran, alat, atau keselamatan kerja di air.`}: `Unit reports include species or lot, time, water parameters, actual feed, mortality, transfers, and approved actions. 給餌量 means “feed amount,” and 水温 means “water temperature.” Unclear units can change a decision; ask for repetition and confirm figures before acting. Distinguish measured data from estimates. The official aquaculture examination is in Japanese, while this material provides an Indonesian bridge through vocabulary and cases. Reading comprehension does not replace training in measurement, equipment, or water-work safety.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Lokasi kolam, tangki, atau keramba memengaruhi pertukaran air, akses kerja, paparan pencemar, dan risiko cuaca. Sarana harus diperiksa menurut rancangan, termasuk jalur orang, pagar, pelampung, pengikatan, serta alat darurat. Jangan masuk air atau menyelam untuk memperbaiki alat tanpa kewenangan dan prosedur khusus. Kerusakan yang tampak kecil dapat membesar karena arus atau beban. Catat unit terdampak dan laporkan sebelum meneruskan kegiatan yang membuat pekerja atau organisme terpapar bahaya.`}:                                                    `The location of a pond, tank, or cage affects water exchange, work access, exposure to contaminants, and weather risks. Inspect facilities according to their design, including walkways, barriers, floats, moorings, and emergency equipment. Do not enter the water or dive to repair equipment without authorization and a specific procedure. A small-looking defect can worsen under current or load. Record the affected unit and report it before continuing work that could expose people or stock to danger.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Pakan dipilih menurut spesies, ukuran, fase, dan rencana produksi. Kondisi air, cuaca, kesehatan, serta respons makan memengaruhi pelaksanaan harian. Pakan berlebih bukan cara pasti mempercepat pertumbuhan; sisa dapat memperburuk lingkungan. Simpan pakan berlabel dan terlindung dari air serta hama. Jangan memberikan produk berjamur atau obat tanpa kewenangan. Catat jumlah aktual dan respons organisme, bukan hanya jatah rencana. Penurunan respons perlu dilaporkan bersama data lingkungan.`}:                                                            `Choose feed according to species, size, life stage, and production plan. Water conditions, weather, health, and feeding response affect daily feeding. Excess feed does not reliably speed growth; leftovers may worsen the environment. Store labeled feed protected from water and pests. Do not use moldy products or administer medication without authorization. Record the amount actually given and the organisms' response, not just the planned ration. Report reduced feeding response together with environmental data.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Pelampung atau alat apung pribadi dipilih, dipakai, dan diperiksa sesuai jenis kerja serta aturan kapal. Alat yang tersedia di lemari tidak melindungi orang yang tidak memakainya saat diwajibkan. Geladak basah, ikan, es, serta gerakan kapal meningkatkan risiko terpeleset dan jatuh. Jaga pijakan, jalur lewat, serta pegangan yang aman. Jangan melewati sisi berbahaya atau duduk di pagar. Perlengkapan tidak boleh mengganggu alat bergerak; kesesuaian dan ukuran diperiksa sebelum operasi.`}:                                                                `Select, wear, and inspect life jackets or personal flotation devices according to the task and vessel rules. Equipment stored in a locker cannot protect someone who is required to wear it but does not. Wet decks, fish, ice, and vessel movement increase slip and fall risks. Maintain secure footing, clear routes, and safe handholds. Do not pass along a hazardous edge or sit on a rail. Protective gear must not interfere with moving equipment; check fit and size before operations.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Perikanan tangkap mengambil organisme dari perairan dengan alat serta metode yang diizinkan. Pengetahuan jenis ikan, musim, daerah operasi, ukuran, dan ketentuan setempat membantu menjaga mutu serta sumber daya. Tugas awak dibagi sesuai instruksi nakhoda dan kompetensi; materi tertulis tidak memberi izin mengemudikan kapal atau mengoperasikan semua alat. Kenali identitas kapal, titik berkumpul, komunikasi, serta peralatan darurat sebelum berangkat. Jangan mengubah lokasi atau alat tangkap tanpa persetujuan yang berwenang.`}:                        `Capture fisheries harvest organisms from the water using permitted gear and methods. Knowing species, seasons, operating areas, sizes, and local rules helps protect product quality and resources. Crew duties are assigned according to the captain's instructions and each person's competence; written material does not authorize anyone to pilot a vessel or operate every type of gear. Before departure, learn the vessel identity, assembly point, communication methods, and emergency equipment. Do not change location or fishing gear without authorized approval.`,
	{field: "ssw.body", source: `Perubahan berenang, nafsu makan, warna, luka, dan kematian dipantau bersama kualitas air serta riwayat kelompok. Gejala tidak cukup untuk menentukan penyakit atau obat sendiri. Mortalitas dicatat menurut unit dan waktu; organisme mati ditangani melalui prosedur fasilitas agar tidak menyebarkan masalah. Pisahkan alat atau kelompok sesuai arahan. Penggunaan obat memerlukan kewenangan serta catatan dan batas penggunaan produk yang berlaku. Jangan mengirim hasil yang statusnya belum dipastikan hanya karena tampak normal dari luar.`}:                   `Monitor changes in swimming, appetite, color, lesions, and mortality together with water quality and lot history. Symptoms alone are not enough to diagnose a disease or choose medication. Record mortality by unit and time; handle dead organisms under facility procedures to avoid spreading a problem. Separate equipment or lots as directed. Medication requires authorization and records, and the product's applicable use limits must be followed. Do not ship products with unconfirmed status just because they look normal externally.`,
}
